ely at the moment so i  just want to finish with this  idea that we can take a systems level  plan of um  output and its sensory feedback and  slowly  pick apart different elements of that  system at the synaptic and neuronal  level  the pre-synaptic gaiting that i didn't  talk about this internal copy system  that eyman has been studying  and then this switching strategy for  alternation  and co-activation that is so important  in  controlling many aspects of motor  behavior so i will stop there  just highlight the people who've done  the work hyman really led  the appropriate spinal neuron project  iman's here in the audience so i would  encourage you to find him and pester him  about more details of that  andrew murray has been leading the  vestibular alternation  co-activation project david ing has been  trying to manipulate chloride currents  and we've been getting a lot of advice  in this system from yensbo nielsen a  human physiologist in denmark  who in a remarkable way predicted  many of the involvements of renshaw  cells and 1a  into neurons on the basis of human  studies and i still don't quite know how  he managed to do that but  everything we are doing is really a  reflection and testing of these human  physiological studies so i'll stop there  thank you very much

